  "tagline": "Blockchain-style database combining MongoDB storage with Tendermint BFT consensus; dormant since 2020.",
  "description": "BigchainDB pairs MongoDB for storage and querying with Tendermint for Byzantine-fault-tolerant consensus, giving a decentralised network of nodes an immutable, append-only record of asset creation and transfer transactions. It was promoted around 2017-2019 as a blockchain database for supply-chain, IP rights and identity projects, overseen by the IPDB Foundation. There has been no release since 2.2.2 in September 2020 and only sporadic commits since, so it is effectively dormant. Ledger needs today are better served by immudb, a permissioned blockchain or an audited Postgres design.",
